  "page1": {
    "title": "Pictures Full of Wishes",
    "subtitle": "Korean folk paintings that carry the dreams of ordinary people.",
    "body": "Long ago, many Koreans painted bright pictures. We call them folk paintings. Plain people made them with love. Each picture held a wish inside it.\n\nA picture of a <u>tiger</u> kept bad luck away. The tiger looked strong and brave. Two magpies brought happy news to a home. People hung them by the door.\n\nA big red flower meant money and a good life. This flower is the peony. A jumping fish stood for hard work and success. Children wished to <mark>pass their tests</mark>.\n\nSo the pictures were full of hope. They were not just pretty. Every line and color carried a dream. Folk paintings still share old wishes today.",
    "illustration": "assets/illustrations/mars/2026-07/15.jpg",
    "illustration_caption": "A tiger, two magpies, a red peony, and a jumping fish — each one carrying a wish."
  },
